      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As you prepare for your journey from London to Paris, remember that the Eurostar is a train, not a train of the kind that would carry a horde of unruly goblins, but it does have its own set of rules, much like the strict codes of conduct in a goblin village. For your luggage, you can bring up to two pieces, each weighing no more than 23kg (50lbs). As for size, the dimensions must not exceed 158cm (62in) in length, 158cm (62in) in width, and 33cm (13in) in height. Keep in mind that these limits are as firm as a goblin's resolve when it comes to their treasure hoard.\n\nNow, regarding your time for check-in at St Pancras, it's best to arrive at least 30 minutes before your train departs. This should give you ample time to navigate through the station, just as a goblin would need time to find the best hiding spot before the humans arrive. Remember, punctuality is as important to humans as it is to goblins when it comes to avoiding unwanted attention. Safe travels, and may your business meetings be as successful as a goblin's heist",
      "source": "target",
